    <h2>What Is the Dairy Queen Swicy Pineapple with Tajín® Blizzard?</h2>
    <p>In one of the most adventurous flavor collaborations in Dairy Queen history, the Swicy Pineapple with Tajín® Blizzard® Treat brings the viral "swicy" (sweet + spicy) culinary trend to the freezer aisle. Built on a foundation of DQ's velvety vanilla soft serve, this limited-edition treat blends real tropical pineapple fruit chunks and syrup with genuine Tajín® Clásico seasoning—the iconic Mexican blend of mild chili peppers, sea salt, and dehydrated lime juice.</p>
    <p>The flavor dynamic is genuinely striking: Dairy Queen's cold soft serve acts as a soothing buffer that tempers the chili heat, allowing the zesty lime and subtle chili warmth to elevate the sweet pineapple rather than overpower it. The result is a vibrant, palate-awakening treat that feels remarkably refreshing in high summer heat.</p>

    <h2>2026 Pricing &amp; Calorie Counts Across All Cup Sizes</h2>
    <p>As part of the Summer 2026 Seasonal Blizzard tier, the Swicy Pineapple Tajín Blizzard is offered across four standard sizes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Mini ($4.49 · ~270 cal):</strong> A 6-ounce portion that provides an adventurous trial run without committing to a full dessert cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Small ($5.29 · 430 cal · 13g Fat):</strong> The sweet spot for single diners—notably standing as the <em>lowest-calorie</em> option among all Summer 2026 seasonals.</li>
      <li><strong>Medium ($6.29 · ~600 cal):</strong> Ideal for hot summer afternoons when you want an extended, cooling citrus-chili refresh.</li>
      <li><strong>Large ($6.99 · ~900 cal):</strong> A generous 21-ounce cup for genuine sweet-and-spicy enthusiasts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Summer 2026 Seasonal Face-Off: How Swicy Pineapple Compares</h2>
    <p>Here is how the Swicy Pineapple Tajín Blizzard stacks up against the rest of Dairy Queen's 2026 summer seasonal roster:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard Treat</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile &amp; Appeal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Swicy Pineapple with Tajín®</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>430</td><td>Sweet pineapple, zesty lime, mild chili warmth; lowest summer calories</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cotton Candy Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>460</td><td>Ultra-sweet, whimsical spun sugar sprinkles; purely sweet profile</td></tr><tr><td><strong>S'mores Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>500</td><td>Campfire comfort: honey-graham crunch, marshmallow creme, fudge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>540</td><td>Decadent bakery richness: cheesecake cubes, strawberry, choco dip</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Tasting Notes &amp; Ordering Recommendations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Is It Truly Spicy?</strong> The heat level is very mild (roughly a 2 out of 10). Tajín's heat comes from mild dried chilis, and the dairy fats in soft serve naturally neutralize capsaicin, leaving primarily tangy lime and warm chili aromatic notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra Tajín Dusting:</strong> If you love street-cart style Mexican fruit cups, ask the crew to add an extra dusting of Tajín seasoning directly over the top curl of your Blizzard (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Best After Savory Mains:</strong> The bright acidity from pineapple and lime cuts exceptionally well through the richness of a <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger">FlameThrower Stackburger</a> or a <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-6pc">6-Piece Chicken Strip Basket</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Seasonal Window:</strong> Available exclusively during Summer 2026, typically from late May through August or while local inventory lasts.</li>
    </ul>

